      "writtenOn": "2019-01-21T08:10:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You could just have said\nansPacket.write((buf.length \u003e\u003e 8) \u0026 0xff);\nansPacket.write(buf.length \u0026 0xff);\nansPacket.write(buf);\n\n\nBut you can also do this in a vastly more efficient way :\n\nfinal byte[] ansPacket \u003d new byte[buf.length + 2];\nansPacket[0] \u003d (buf.length \u003e\u003e 8) \u0026 0xff;\nansPacket[1] \u003d buf.length \u0026 0xff;\nSystem.arrayCopy(buf, 0, ansPacket, 2, buf.length);\nreturn ansPacket;",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 299,
        "startChar": 8,
